# WebSocket Architecture Analysis & Proposed UI Events WebSocket Plan

## Current WebSocket Channels Analysis

| Channel Name | Backend Endpoint | Connection Manager | UI Responsibility |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Clipboard WS** | `/ws/clipboard` | `ClipboardConnectionManager` | Dedicated strictly to **text/clipboard history sync** across devices (`refreshClipboardHistory()`). Does **NOT** touch file list UI. |
| **File Events WS** | `/ws/file_events` | `FileEventsConnectionManager` | Dedicated to **real-time file system mutations** (`mkdir`, `rename`, `delete`, `upload`). Triggers `refreshFileList('ws_file_change')`. |
| **Upload Status WS** | `/ws/upload-status` | `UploadStatusManager` | Dedicated to **live file transfer progress tracking** (bytes, speed, percentage). |

### Finding
The Clipboard WebSocket (`/ws/clipboard`) is **already cleanly isolated** and is **never used** to update file list UI elements.

However, if you want a **new dedicated WebSocket channel specifically for custom UI operations** (e.g., system toasts, device presence, custom UI state sync, or layout updates without triggering file refreshes), we can introduce a new **`UI Events WebSocket`**.

